  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "reasoning",
        "score": 4,
        "rationale": "The agent correctly separates 'I couldn't list secrets' from 'the secret is confirmed missing', and it correctly says the PAT is needed because events made with GITHUB_TOKEN don't trigger downstream workflows; but it never explains why the startup fails (CMS_E2E_PAT is a required input that the consumer caller has to bind), it calls Issues and Actions part of a 'standard set' instead of saying which API each one covers, and its two permission tables contradict each other and include unsupported extras."
      },
